## What is AI Buildspace?

AI Buildspace is a place for people who build with AI, not just talk about it. Every post here documents something I actually shipped, a workflow that saved hours, a prompt pattern that stopped hallucinating, or a pipeline that scaled beyond a toy demo.

If you found this site through a YouTube Short or a LinkedIn post, welcome. You are in the right place.

## What you will find here

The content falls into a few buckets:

- **Workflow breakdowns.** Step-by-step looks at AI automations running in real projects.
- **Prompt engineering patterns.** Techniques that work across models and hold up under adversarial inputs.
- **Tool comparisons.** Honest takes on what actually ships versus what demos well at conferences.
- **Multi-agent design.** How to coordinate agents without turning your codebase into spaghetti.

## The philosophy

Most AI content optimises for views. A clever demo gets clicks. A nuanced "this works in these conditions, not those" post does not trend.

This site optimises for builders. That means:

> If I have not shipped it, I do not write about it.

The bar is: could someone read this post on a Monday morning and use it to finish something real by Friday? If yes, it ships. If not, it stays in drafts.

## How to follow along

Posts go up whenever something is worth sharing. The fastest way to stay up to date is via the [YouTube channel](https://www.youtube.com/@ropats16) where short-form walkthroughs accompany each written piece.

You can also dig into older content from the blog index. Start with the workflow breakdowns if you are new, and jump to prompt engineering if you have been building with LLMs for a while.

